      "content": "For cooling cooked poultry, you must follow a strict two-stage cooling process to keep *Clostridium perfringens* in check. The first stage requires cooling the poultry from its initial temperature down to $70^\\circ\\text{F}$ ($21^\\circ\\text{C}$) within two hours. After that, you must rapidly cool it from $70^\\circ\\text{F}$ ($21^\\circ\\text{C}$) down to $41^\\circ\\text{F}$ ($5^\\circ\\text{C}$) within the next four hours. This two-stage cooling ensures the temperature drops quickly enough to prevent the dangerous growth of pathogens.",
